The Orin Nano was booted from SD card.
The original installation was a Jetson Jetpack 7.2 install with 6.8.12-1021-tegra.

1. We borrowed the kernel - copied the /lib/modules/6.8.12-1021-tegra + /boot/Image to another place. The dtb/kernel_tegra234-p3768-0000+p3767-0005-nv-super.dtb and the initrd was also copied - althrough replaced later.
2. Used the Armbian UEFI-arm64 image as a base.
3. Did test booting the stock Armbian image - nothing happened after GRUB.

4. The armbi_root partition is emptied out via rm -rf and a Alpine Linux edge bootstrap tar.xz was extracted onto the partition. Chroot was used to install some base packages as listed in world. /boot was kept for the GRUB config.
5. Image is copied to /boot, DTB too as filename dtb, and initrd as a first boot test. Modules copied to /lib/modules. The stock Armbian grub dir was copied and filenames edited.
	  echo	'Loading Linux Nvidia kernel ...'
	  linux	/boot/vmlinuz root=UUID=5247d3a2-cb57-41fa-89cc-d75502121d5e console=tty1 splash plymouth.ignore-serial-consoles rw rootwait rootfstype=ext4 mminit_loglevel=4 console=ttyTCU0,115200 firmware_class.path=/lib/firmware fbcon=map:0 video=efifb:off efi_pstore.pstore_disable=1 pstore.backend=ramoops efi=runtime pci=pcie_bus_perf nvme.use_threaded_interrupts=1
	  echo	'Loading initial ramdisk ...'
	  initrd	/boot/initramfs
    devicetree ...
6. The installation did not boot with devicetree. Apparently loading the jetson DTB actually causes the board to brown out.
7. devicetree was removed and the board boots fine over ACPI with no DTB loaded by GRUB.

8. Nvidia OoT firmware from the BSP is installed into /lib/firmware.
Only nvidia-l4t-firmware was used. For Nvgpu package is a stub and Openrm is not used by the kernel.
